            <title>[LU-21285] sanity-sec test_48d: truncate of encrypted file fails with EOPNOTSUPP when read ahead page is still locked</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21285</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Patrickbot &amp;lt;patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/fb852cf2-0bb6-4701-8ddc-99d6521a3a03" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/fb852cf2-0bb6-4701-8ddc-99d6521a3a03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_48d failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;truncate /mnt/lustre/d48d.sanity-sec/f48d.sanity-sec to 8404999 failed
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.62.1&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137384" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137384&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 5.14.0-687.60.1.el9_8.aarch64+64k&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Server&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.62.1&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137384" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137384&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 4.18.0-553.177.1.el8_10_lustre.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sanity-sec test_48d (added by &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20964" title="Client LBUG/kernel panic: ASSERTION( page-&amp;gt;cp_owner != NULL ) in cl_page_list_add via ll_io_zero_page during ftruncate of fscrypt-encrypted file" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20964"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20964&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) fails with "truncate ... failed: Operation not supported" when the page being zeroed is still locked by in-flight read ahead.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Failed session: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/c31d3160-ba79-4457-9009-9dad79900597" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/c31d3160-ba79-4457-9009-9dad79900597&lt;/a&gt; (review-ldiskfs-arm, rocky9.8 aarch64 client, 64K pages, change 70663 ps4 build 137384).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Analysis from the client debug log: ll_setattr_raw() sends the truncate to the MDT, then ll_io_zero_page() runs for page 128. It takes the PW lock (matched) and calls get_folio_nowait() with FGP_NOWAIT, which fails if the page is locked, and the function returns -EOPNOTSUPP (llite_lib.c, "IS_ERR_OR_NULL(folio)" case). ll_setattr_raw() fails the truncate with it. The read ahead RPCs of the test's dd were still completing at that moment (OST_READ replies at ...145.406 and ...145.834, after the truncate at ...145.26), so the read ahead pages were still locked. The test's "sleep 1" is not enough on a slow client, and the kernel returns EOPNOTSUPP to the application for what is only a transient page lock.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Only failure of 48d in 30 days (about 1 of 55 runs on review-ldiskfs-arm, 0 of 9395 suite runs elsewhere), and not caused by change 70663: that change does not touch the setattr or zero page path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible fixes: have ll_io_zero_page() wait for the page lock (or retry) instead of returning -EOPNOTSUPP, and/or wait for read ahead to finish in the test instead of a fixed sleep.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Related: &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20964" title="Client LBUG/kernel panic: ASSERTION( page-&amp;gt;cp_owner != NULL ) in cl_page_list_add via ll_io_zero_page during ftruncate of fscrypt-encrypted file" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20964"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20964&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (merged, added ll_io_zero_page() keeping the zero page owned and test 48d).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-70663-ps4-14d32ec52f14 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/70663" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/70663&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
